Files taken from zakuro/src, and what we changed in them:
- audio.rs, gamepad.rs, input.rs, microphone.rs, present.rs, pro_controller.rs: as-is (present.rs plus `set_vsync`; input.rs's
  tests use the new default keys), except `zakuro_core::` became
  `xr_hle::` (our port of zakuro-core).
- settings.rs: the same, plus: the `recompiled` setting (3dsrecomp's code vs the interpreter) is removed from Settings and
  GameSettings; the file lives in <config dir>/redex/settings.toml instead of .../zakuro/; the GPU resolution defaults
  to 2x instead of 3x.
- lib.rs: rewritten from Zakuro's lib.rs, keeping its window/backend setup (`resumed`), event handling, key handling
  (F1, F9, F10, F11, Tab fast forward, M to blow into the mic), touch and tilt, frame pacing (`step`, FRAME_TIME,
  CATCH_UP_LIMIT, MAX_SKIPPED, `skips_showing` and its test), `emulate`, `present`, `shown` and `shown_right`, and its
  interface wiring: egui fed the window's events (`window_event`, `pointer_taken`), the key rebinding in
  `key`, `poll_gamepads` (Home), `apply_settings`, `apply_microphone`, `interface` and the game's keyboard.
  Changes:
  - one game, booted through a closure the runtime passes (`run(options, config, boot)`), driven through the `Game`
    trait (run_frame + system) instead of owning a zakuro_core::System; the window's thread holds the executor's
    baton between frames;
  - Escape pauses (as Azahar's does) instead of opening Zakuro's menu over the game; Home on a controller opens and
    closes Configure;
  - a native menu bar like Azahar's (menubar.rs, our own, on the `muda` crate): File, Emulation (pause, restart, speed
    limit, Configure), View (fullscreen, layouts, swap screens, rotate, FPS), Tools (screenshot, texture packs),
    Multiplayer (disabled, coming soon), Help (about, GitHub page); F12 saves a screenshot; on Windows only for now
    (muda is a Windows-only dependency, other systems get a stub and use the keys and Configure);
  - a speed limit (Azahar's limit speed, 60-500% or unlocked) and VSync on/off; swap screens in every layout
    (the presenter's StackedSwapped, SideBySideSwapped and LargeBottom arrangements in our zakuro-gpu copy);
  - Restart starts the game again in a new process with the same command line;
  - the window is titled "RE:DEX — Pokémon X" and has the RE:DEX gear (assets/icon.png) as its window and taskbar icon;
  - audio.rs: the sound ramps back in over about 5 ms after a gap (a pause, Configure, a menu), so it doesn't click;
  - the window can stop after N frames (`Options::frames`); the window title shows RE:DEX and the frame count.
- gui.rs: as-is, without the system fonts for Japanese, Korean and Chinese game names (the menus show none).
- menus.rs: Zakuro's settings window rebuilt as Azahar's Configure dialog with General / Graphics / Audio / Controls
  tabs, from Zakuro's helper rows (resolution, texture packs, interpolation, window scale, screens, rotation, filter,
  integer scale, top shape, 3D, depth, language), its controls and controller grids, `keyboard` (the game's text
  entry), `message`, the frame rate and fast forward badges, and its tests ("the settings fit a short screen", "a long
  message can still be closed", "keys have short names"). Our own on top: the RE:DEX theme (the icon's red, dark and
  light following Windows or chosen), switches, group boxes, the toasts, the FPS pill, the paused look, and animations
  (Configure fading and scaling in and out, the tab underline gliding, hover easing, toasts sliding, the screenshot
  flash), which stay still when Windows' "Show animations" is off.
- settings.rs: also vsync, limit_speed, speed_limit and swap_screens; a PC keyboard layout for new installs (WASD
  circle pad, arrows D-pad, Space A, Q B, F X, R Y, 1 L, 3 R, Z ZL, C ZR, IJKL C-stick; saved files keep their keys);
  REDEX_SETTINGS points the settings at another file (tests).
- Left out (not ported): the library, recompile.rs and zig.rs (3dsrecomp builds; to be replaced by our xr-recomp) and
  the compiler offer, cheats, multiplayer and rooms, Download Play, per-game settings (game_settings), the library
  background, report.rs, camera.rs (nokhwa), cli.rs, save states (F5/F8), replays (ZAKURO_RECORD/REPLAY), the test
  pattern, the GameOverlay hook.
Nothing from fearkov/3dsrecomp (recomp3ds, recomp-abi) is used.

